 -- Function: df_summarize (T, NAME1, FN1, NAME2, FN2, ...)
     Reduce a table to a single-row summary.  Takes alternating
     name/lambda pairs.  Each lambda receives whole columns (as ndarray
     or string-column handles) and must return a scalar.

     Also works with grouped tables from ‘df_group_by’, producing one
     row per group.

* Menu:

     * Examples::

1.3.1.26 Examples
.................

(%i1) df_summarize(T, "avg", lambda([price], np_mean(price)),
                      "n",   lambda([price], df_count(price)));
(%o1)              df_table: 1 rows x 2 cols

